pecialized Working Groups\nSWG Grants\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2026\nLeft Sidebar\n2 min read · January 27, 2026\nJanuary 27, 2026\nShare\nSWG Grants\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2026\nBoosting the immune therapy efficacy with proteasome inhibitors in Mantle Cell Lymphoma\nIntegrative transcriptomic and preclinical modelling to identify targetable signaling axes in chronic myelomonocytic leukemia\nLongitudinal immunomics of VEXAS/MDS: a study on behalf of the EHA MDS-SWG\nDecoding CLL Immunogenetics: A Global Study to Refine Disease Biology and Patient Stratification (SWG on European Research Initiative on CLL (ERIC))\nExpanding the genetic landscape of platelet reactivity modifiers in hemophilia: a multi-center study\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2025\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2024\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2023\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2026\nFrom August to October, 2025, SWGs were invited to develop project ideas and apply for a 2026 SWG Grant.\nFor the 2026 call, EHA offered five grants, each worth €30,000.\nApplications\nWe received 25 different applications from nine SWGs. This was ten more applications than we received in 2024 and fourteen more than in 2023.\nThese applications came from the:\nSWG on Adult Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) (1 application)\nSWG on Aging in Hematology (1 application)\nSWG on Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) (1 application)\nSWG on European Research Initiative on CLL (ERIC) (1 application)\nSWG on Immune Therapies for Hematologic Disorders (2 applications)\nSWG on Infections in Hematology (1 application)\nSWG on Myelodysplastic Syndromes (MDS) (7 applications)\nSWG on Myelodysplastic Syndromes (MDS) and Red Cells and Iron Joint Application (1 application)\nSWG on Myeloproliferative Neoplasms (MPN) (3 applications)\nSWG on Quality of Life and Symptoms (QLS) (1 application)\nSWG on Red Cells and Iron (3 applications)\nSWG on Thrombocytopenias and Platelet Function Disorders (TPFD) (2 applications)\nSWG on Transfusion and Bleeding & Thrombosis Joint Application (1 application)\nWinners\nAll applications were reviewed against our selection criteria by SWG Committee members. These criteria are explained on the main SWG Grants page.\nAfter careful consideration and fruitful discussion, the SWG Committee chose the following winners:\nBoosting the immune therapy efficacy with proteasome inhibitors in Mantle Cell Lymphoma (SWG on Immune Therapies for Hematologic Disorders)\nDecoding CLL Immunogenetics: A Global Study to Refine Disease Biology and Patient Stratification (SWG on European Research Initiative on CLL (ERIC))\nExpanding the genetic landscape of platelet reactivity modifiers in hemophilia: a multi-center study (SWG on Thrombocytopenias and Platelet Function Disorders (TPFD))\nIntegrative transcriptomic and preclinical modelling to identify targetable signaling axes in chronic myelomonocytic leukemia (SWG on Myelodysplastic Syndromes (MDS))\nLongitudinal immunomics of VEXAS/MDS: a study on behalf of the EHA MDS-SWG (SWG on Myelodysplastic Syndromes (MDS))\nShare\nSWG Grants\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2026\nBoosting the immune therapy efficacy with proteasome inhibitors in Mantle Cell Lymphoma\nIntegrative transcriptomic and preclinical modelling to identify targetable signaling axes in chronic myelomonocytic leukemia\nLongitudinal immunomics of VEXAS/MDS: a study on behalf of the EHA MDS-SWG\nDecoding CLL Immunogenetics: A Global Study to Refine Disease Biology and Patient Stratification (SWG on European Research Initiative on CLL (ERIC))\nExpanding the genetic landscape of platelet reactivity modifiers in hemophilia: a multi-center study\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2025\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2024\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2023\nJoin EHA\nFull membership\nJunior membership\n60-day trial\nGet involved\nCareer development\nScientific meetings\nAbout us\nMission and vision\nJobs\nSponsor EHA\nContact us\nFollow us\nPrivacy statement\nTerms and conditions\nSubscribe\nCopyright © 